 64: ## Quick Start
 65: 
 66: ### Prerequisites
 67: - [Claude Code](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup) installed and configured
 68: - Git for version control
 69: - Node.js 18+ (or your preferred runtime)
 70: - Operating Systems: macOS 10.15+, Ubuntu 20.04+/Debian 10+, or Windows 10+ (with WSL 1, WSL 2, or Git for Windows)
 71: - Hardware: 4GB+ RAM
 72: 
 73: ### Setup your new project with ClaudeKit
 74: 
 75: 1. **Install ClaudeKit CLI**:
 76:    ```bash
 77:    npm install -g claudekit-cli
 78:    ```
 79: 
 80: 2. **Create your new project with ClaudeKit framework**:
 81:    ```bash
 82:    mkdir my-project
 83:    ck new --dir my-project --kit engineer
 84:    ```
 85: 
 86:    **Note:** If you want to use the kit with your existing project:
 87:    ```bash
 88:    cd /path/to/project
 89:    ck init --kit engineer
 90:    ```
 91: 
 92:    To target another provider later, run ClaudeKit CLI migration from the project root, for example:
 93:    ```bash
 94:    ck migrate -a opencode
 95:    ```
 96: 
 97: 3. **Start development**:
 98:    ```bash
 99:    # Begin with Claude Code
100:    claude
101:    # [YOLO mode - not recommended]
102:    # claude --dangerously-skip-permissions
103: 
104:    # now you can use these specific commands
105:    /ck:plan "implement user authentication"
106:    /ck:plan --deep "refactor the notification pipeline"
107:    /ck:plan --tdd "refactor auth middleware safely"
108:    /ck:cook "add database integration"
109:    /ck:cook "refactor auth middleware" --tdd
110:    ```
111: 
112: 📖 **Learn more from our docs:** [https://docs.claudekit.cc](https://docs.claudekit.cc)
113: 
114: ## Local Scripts (Usage)
115: 
116: This repository is self-contained — run every command from this repo with no other checkout required.
117: 
118: | Command | What it does |
119: |---------|--------------|
120: | `npm run lint` | Content lint for kit skills. Diff-based: violations on files changed vs the base ref are errors (exit 1); legacy/unchanged files are warnings (exit 0). Reuses the in-repo frontmatter validator. |
121: | `npm test` | Hook/script unit tests (`node --test`) plus the chrome-profile Python check. |
122: | `npm run test:eval` / `:e2e` / `:judge` / `:all` | Skill eval tiers (smoke / E2E / LLM-judge / full). |
123: 
124: Lint severity uses `git diff --name-only <base>...HEAD`, where base is `LINT_BASE_REF` (set by CI) or `origin/dev` locally; if no base ref is available it degrades to warn-only.
