  79: ## 📦 What's Included
  80: 
  81: This repository provides **177 scientific and research skills** organized into the following categories:
  82: 
  83: - **100+ Scientific & Financial Databases** - The [Database Lookup](skills/database-lookup/SKILL.md) skill documents 80 databases with public, registered, or licensed access (PubChem, ChEMBL, UniProt, COSMIC, ClinicalTrials.gov, FRED, USPTO, and more), including endpoint selection, pagination, and provenance. Dedicated skills cover DepMap, Imaging Data Commons, PrimeKG, NCATS ARAX, U.S. Treasury Fiscal Data, Hugging Science, OneKGPd, Genomic Intelligence, and AlphaGenome. Multi-database packages such as BioServices, Biopython, and gget add further coverage
  84: - **70+ Optimized Python Package Skills** - Explicitly defined, version-aware workflows for RDKit, Scanpy, PyTorch Lightning, scikit-learn, PyTDC, PathML, pydicom, NeuroKit2, PufferLib, QuTiP, GeoPandas, pymatgen, BioPython, Qiskit, Molecular Dynamics (OpenMM/MDAnalysis), and others. The agent can still use *any* Python package; these skills provide stronger, safer guidance for the packages listed
  85: - **9 Scientific Integration Skills** - Explicitly defined skills for Benchling, DNAnexus, LatchBio, OMERO, Protocols.io, Open Notebook, Ginkgo Cloud Lab, LabArchives, and Opentrons. Again, the agent is not limited to these — any API or platform reachable from Python is fair game; these skills are the optimized, pre-documented paths
  86: - **30+ Analysis & Communication Tools** - Literature review, evidence-traceable scientific writing, confidential peer review, document processing, Paperclip (full-text papers, FDA/PMDA/EMA filings, and trial registries with line-pinned citations), Paperzilla, Exa Search, macro-free PPTX posters, slides, schematics, infographics, Mermaid diagrams, and more
  87: - **10+ Research & Clinical Tools** - Evidence-bounded hypothesis generation, grant writing, aggregate clinical decision-support research, clinician-authored treatment-plan formatting, PK/PD modelling and simulation (NCA, population PK, exposure-response, bioequivalence, first-in-human dose), BIDS, ISO standards-readiness evidence preparation (ISO 13485, ISO 14971, ISO/IEC 17025, ISO 15189), analytical method validation and transfer (ICH Q2(R2)/Q14, ICH M10, USP, CLSI EP), scenario analysis, and workflow-derived skill drafting with Autoskill
