 779: ### Testing
 780: 
 781: Every skill that ships `scripts/` must have a test suite under `tests/<skill-name>/` and an entry in [`tests/skill-requirements.toml`](tests/skill-requirements.toml). The `tests/_meta` guard checks this coverage and the shared structural contract: frontmatter, document length, local links, script syntax, bytecode, and hardcoded local paths. It also validates `plugin.json` against the bundled Agent Plugins schema and checks that its version matches `pyproject.toml`. CLI `--help` and worked-example execution checks belong to the individual skill suites.
 782: 
 783: ```bash
 784: # Install repository development and validation tools
 785: uv sync
 786: 
 787: # Structural contract and coverage guard — seconds, no scientific packages needed
 788: uv run python -m pytest tests/_meta -q
 789: 
 790: # Validate one skill's Agent Skills frontmatter
 791: uv run skills-ref validate skills/<skill-name>
 792: 
 793: # One skill's suite in the current environment
 794: uv run --with pytest python -m pytest tests/<skill-name> -q
 795: 
 796: # One skill with its declared packages and Python version
 797: uv run python tests/run_all.py --isolated <skill-name>
 798: 
 799: # Every suite, each in its own throwaway environment
 800: uv run python tests/run_all.py --isolated
 801: ```
 802: 
 803: Run one skill per pytest process: different skills reuse module names such as `_common`, so collecting several suites together can import the wrong module. `tests/run_all.py` handles process isolation; `--isolated` also provides each skill's declared dependency environment. A suite run in the current environment may skip checks when required packages are absent.
 804: 
 805: The [Skill Tests](https://github.com/K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills/actions/workflows/skill-tests.yml) workflow runs the contract and standard-library-only suites for relevant pull requests and pushes to `main`, and can be triggered manually. The full scientific dependency sweep is not run in CI; run it before a release or when changing the shared contract. Some skills need external runtimes or system tools; installation gaps are documented in [`tests/skill-requirements.toml`](tests/skill-requirements.toml).
 806: 
 807: ### Security Scanning
 808: 
 809: All skills in this repository are security-scanned using [Cisco AI Defense Skill Scanner](https://github.com/cisco-ai-defense/skill-scanner), an open-source tool that detects prompt injection, data exfiltration, and malicious code patterns in Agent Skills.
 810: 
 811: If you are contributing a new skill, we recommend running the scanner locally before submitting a pull request:
 812: 
 813: ```bash
 814: uv pip install cisco-ai-skill-scanner
 815: skill-scanner scan /path/to/your/skill --use-behavioral
 816: ```
 817: 
 818: > **Note:** A clean scan result reduces noise in review, but does not guarantee a skill is free of all risk. Contributed skills are also reviewed manually before merging.
