 868: ## ❓ FAQ
 869: 
 870: ### General Questions
 871: 
 872: **Q: Is this free to use?**  
 873: A: Yes! This repository is MIT licensed. However, each individual skill has its own license specified in the `license` metadata field within its `SKILL.md` file—be sure to review and comply with those terms.
 874: 
 875: **Q: Why are all skills grouped together instead of separate packages?**  
 876: A: We believe good science in the age of AI is inherently interdisciplinary. Bundling all skills together makes it trivial for you (and your agent) to bridge across fields—e.g., combining genomics, cheminformatics, clinical data, and machine learning in one workflow—without worrying about which individual skills to install or wire together.
 877: 
 878: **Q: Can I use this for commercial projects?**  
 879: A: The repository itself is MIT licensed, which allows commercial use. However, individual skills may have different licenses—check the `license` field in each skill's `SKILL.md` file to ensure compliance with your intended use.
 880: 
 881: **Q: Do all skills have the same license?**  
 882: A: No. Each skill has its own license specified in the `license` metadata field within its `SKILL.md` file. These licenses may differ from the repository's MIT License. Users are responsible for reviewing and adhering to the license terms of each individual skill they use.
 883: 
 884: **Q: How often is this updated?**  
 885: A: We regularly update skills to reflect the latest versions of packages and APIs. Major updates are announced in release notes.
 886: 
 887: **Q: Can I use this with other AI models?**  
 888: A: The core `SKILL.md` format follows the open [Agent Skills](https://agentskills.io/) standard. Installation paths, discovery, and optional metadata support vary by host and version, so confirm your target host's current documentation.
 889: 
 890: ### Installation & Setup
 891: 
 892: **Q: Do I need all the Python packages installed?**  
 893: A: No. Install only the dependencies for the workflows you use, following each `SKILL.md`. Keep workflows with incompatible package or Python requirements in separate environments.
 894: 
 895: **Q: What if a skill doesn't work?**  
 896: A: First check the [Troubleshooting](#-troubleshooting) section. If the issue persists, file an issue on GitHub with detailed reproduction steps.
 897: 
 898: **Q: Do the skills work offline?**  
 899: A: Local analysis can work offline once its dependencies, reference data, and model files are available. Database queries, hosted models, and cloud platforms need network access; check the individual skill's requirements.
 900: 
 901: ### Contributing
 902: 
 903: **Q: Can I contribute my own skills?**  
 904: A: Absolutely! We welcome contributions. See the [Contributing](#-contributing) section for guidelines and best practices.
 905: 
 906: **Q: How do I report bugs or suggest features?**  
 907: A: Open an issue on GitHub with a clear description. For bugs, include reproduction steps and expected vs actual behavior.
