59: ## Claude API
60: 
61: You can use Anthropic's pre-built skills, and upload custom skills, via the Claude API. See the [Skills API Quickstart](https://docs.claude.com/en/api/skills-guide#creating-a-skill) for more.
62: 
63: # Creating a Basic Skill
64: 
65: Skills are simple to create - just a folder with a `SKILL.md` file containing YAML frontmatter and instructions. You can use the **template-skill** in this repository as a starting point:
66: 
67: ```markdown
68: ---
69: name: my-skill-name
70: description: A clear description of what this skill does and when to use it
71: ---
72: 
73: # My Skill Name
74: 
75: [Add your instructions here that Claude will follow when this skill is active]
76: 
77: ## Examples
78: - Example usage 1
79: - Example usage 2
80: 
81: ## Guidelines
82: - Guideline 1
83: - Guideline 2
84: ```
85: 
86: The frontmatter requires only two fields:
87: - `name` - A unique identifier for your skill (lowercase, hyphens for spaces)
88: - `description` - A complete description of what the skill does and when to use it
89: 
90: The markdown content below contains the instructions, examples, and guidelines that Claude will follow. For more details, see [How to create custom skills](https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12512198-creating-custom-skills).
